'''''Semele''''' is a [[genus (biology)|genus]] of [[flowering plant]]s native to the [[Canary Islands]] and [[Madeira]].<ref name=wcspf/> In the [[APG III system|APG III classification system]], it is placed in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Asparagaceae]], subfamily [[Convallarioideae]] (formerly the family [[Ruscaceae]]).<ref>{{Citation |last=Chase |first=M.W. |last2=Reveal |first2=J.L. |last3=Fay |first3=M.F. |year=2009 |title=A subfamilial classification for the expanded asparagalean families Amaryllidaceae, Asparagaceae and Xanthorrhoeaceae |journal=Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society |volume=161 |issue=2 |pages=132–136 |doi=10.1111/j.1095-8339.2009.00999.x|name-list-style=amp |doi-access=free }}</ref>

Three species are recognized:<ref name=wcspf/>

*''[[Semele androgyna]]'' <small>(L.) Kunth</small> - [[Canary Islands]] and [[Madeira]]
*''[[Semele gayae]]'' <small>(Webb & Berthel.) Svent. & Kunkel</small> - [[Gran Canaria]]
*''[[Semele menezesii]]'' <small>J.G.Costa</small> - [[Madeira]]

